Multicast Delegates:
•	A multicast delegate in C# is a delegate that can hold references to multiple methods and invoke them one after another in a single call.
•	A multicast delegate is a delegate that points to more than one method and executes all of them in sequence when invoked.
•	For example, in a class if multiple methods with same signature we can call all methods by using same delegate
•	Suppose the methods with same return type first result will be override by the next result and you will get the last result only. rather if it is a void returning no problem.
•	It is always better when you are using multicast delegate the methods should be non value returning
